00:28:02.721 --> 00:28:08.904
From GitHub Blog: How to choose the next safe step in application modernization.

00:28:09.009 --> 00:28:15.106
A request to modernize an application often starts with a technology question: Which framework

00:28:15.106 --> 00:28:21.723
should replace the old one? Before you choose, find out what still works. Then

00:28:21.723 --> 00:28:26.084
collect evidence that can act as a regression net for that behavior and show

00:28:26.084 --> 00:28:33.390
where modernization is necessary. I used an evidence-first method on four public applications, from

00:28:33.390 --> 00:28:39.181
a small Node.js game to a large Java enterprise resource planning (ERP)

00:28:39.181 --> 00:28:45.626
application. Each needed a different treatment, but the way I collected evidence, chose the

00:28:45.626 --> 00:28:52.195
next experiment, and decided on possible proof points was repeatable. This post walks through

00:28:52.195 --> 00:28:56.664
that process so you can apply it to one application of your own.

